<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Key technical decisions =
explained</strong>:</p>
<ol class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Operational Transformat=
ion</strong>: Chose OT over CRDT for simpler implementation and better perf=
ormance with text editing</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Optimistic Updates</str=
ong>: Apply changes immediately for responsive UX, then handle conflicts</l=
i>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>WebSocket Architecture<=
/strong>: Direct connection for low latency, with fallback to HTTP polling<=
/li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Cursor Synchronization<=
/strong>: Real-time cursor sharing for better collaboration awareness</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Memory Management</stro=
ng>: Bounded operation history to prevent memory leaks</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">This implementation handles the =
core challenges of real-time collaboration while maintaining excellent perf=
ormance and user experience.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Ex=
cellent implementation! I'm particularly impressed by your operational tran=
sformation logic and the way you handle optimistic updates. Your approach t=
o conflict resolution and the cursor synchronization is very thoughtful.</p=
>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Let me ask you about one more th=
ing before we wrap up. How would you handle the performance implications if=
 this collaborative editor needed to support very large documents - say, 10=
MB+ text files with hundreds of simultaneous users? What changes would you =
make to your architecture?</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: That=
's an excellent question that touches on some of the most challenging aspec=
ts of collaborative editing at scale! Let me outline the key architectural =
changes I'd make:</p>
